# Copy to .env.dev (gitignored) to run `make dev-production` against a real GitHub
# instead of the fake one (tests/github_fake.py). It needs BOTH apps, all seven
# variables below: with none of them set (no .env.dev, or every line commented out)
# the fake serves both apps, with a generated key, secrets and fixture repos; a
# partial set stops `make dev-production` with a message naming what is missing.
# Use dev apps, not the production ones: each holds this instance's callback URLs.

# --- The OAuth App (sign-in) ---------------------------------------------------
# Callback URL: http://whygraph.localhost:5173/auth/github
WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=replace-me
# A file holding the client secret, outside the repo, readable only by you (chmod 600).
WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE=$HOME/.whygraph-dev-oauth-secret

# --- The GitHub App (projects) -------------------------------------------------
# Settings: repository permissions Contents, Metadata, Pull requests and Issues
# read-only; the FIRST callback URL http://whygraph.localhost:5173/auth/github-app;
# "Request user authorization (OAuth) during installation", "Expire user
# authorization tokens" and "Redirect on update" on; webhook active with a secret of
# at least 32 characters, events Push and Repository (see the webhook relay below).
# The app's URL name (github.com/apps/<slug>).
WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_APP_SLUG=replace-me
WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=replace-me
# Files outside the repo, chmod 600: the client secret, the app's private key (the
# .pem GitHub generates) and the webhook secret.
WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE=$HOME/.whygraph-dev-app-secret
WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=$HOME/.whygraph-dev-app-key.pem
WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET_FILE=$HOME/.whygraph-dev-webhook-secret

# Webhooks: GitHub cannot reach whygraph.localhost, so relay them through a
# smee.io channel. Set the app's webhook URL to https://smee.io/<channel>, then
# run beside `make dev-production`:
#   npx smee-client -u https://smee.io/<channel> -t http://whygraph.localhost:5173/github/webhook
# (through Vite, which keeps the base host the portal requires; without the relay
# pushes still arrive through the hourly reconcile and "Scan now").

# Only for GitHub Enterprise Server; the defaults are github.com.
# WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_URL=https://github.com
# WHYGRAPH_GITHUB_API_URL=https://api.github.com
